course: dictionary
lesson: 2354
title: Words from places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where a person or thing comes from. Cuban means from Cuba, an island country in the Caribbean Sea, south of Florida. Because it comes from the name of a place, it always starts with a capital letter.
explain: A Cuban is a person from Cuba. So Cuban can be a describing word, like Cuban music, or a name for a person, like a Cuban. Read the words around it to see which job it does. «Salsa grew up in New York and the Caribbean from Cuban and Puerto Rican music.» Here Cuban describes the music.
explain: When you meet a word like this, check the sentence. Put in your meaning, from Cuba, and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: Cuban means from Cuba. Cuba is an island country in the Caribbean Sea, south of Florida.
fact: A Cuban is a person from Cuba. The plural is Cubans.
fact: Cuba's capital city is Havana, and people there speak Spanish.
fact: Cuban music such as salsa and son, Cuban dance, food and old cars are famous around the world.
fact: The Cuban Missile Crisis of 1962 was when the USA and the Soviet Union came close to nuclear war. Cuban always has a capital C.
exercise: What is the capital city of Cuba? | Miami | New York | Key West | *Havana
exercise: «Salsa grew up in New York and the Caribbean from Cuban and Puerto Rican music.» Find the word that tells you where the music comes from. | New | grew | *Cuban | Salsa
exercise: Why does Cuban start with a capital C? | *Because it comes from the name of a place, Cuba | Because it is the first word of every sentence | Because it is a long word | Because it is a dance
test: What does a Cuban mean? | A kind of sweet food | A Spanish dance | *A person from Cuba | A type of old car
test: In which sea is Cuba found? | The Dead Sea | *The Caribbean Sea | The North Sea | The Red Sea
exam: Which is the best reason to write Cuban with a capital C? | It is a longer word than most | Every adjective starts with a capital letter | It sounds louder when spoken | *Cuban comes from the place name Cuba, so it is a word about a place
